# Workspace CLI installed acceptance handoff

Client source: 8f4dd72cb9c6c58c0860bb9125289986cfc180d1 in /root/lane-rel-cloud.
Do not change that clean tree until the client build is captured.
The binary manifest is created only by a successful build-client.sh.
A missing manifest or build.exit=75 is a blocked preparation, not a binary or acceptance result.

## Entries

- build-client.sh: nonblocking global/SCI/lane locks, disk and raw MemFree admission,
  offline Linux amd64 static build with VCS metadata, startup/help checks and SHA-256.
- client/ownsolid and client/client-manifest.json: successful build outputs only.
- installed_workspaces.py: installed public API acceptance, no new services or database.
- test_installed_workspaces.py: eight input/provenance/privacy/diagnostic guard tests.

The acceptance driver needs Linux root, Python 3.12 standard library, util-linux
nsenter/unshare/mount, the executable client and the existing DEL installation PID.
Its input directory is the actual DEL runtime-evidence directory. It must contain:
installed-ready.json, installed-provenance.json, installed-control.bin,
installation-ca.pem, admin-credential, person.json and scope-state.json.
All JSON and credential inputs retain owner-only mode 0600 in a mode 0700 directory.
The administrator email is read from the generated credential request. No account,
password, origin, CA or workspace identifier has a default in the runner.

Run only in the installation owner's existing Linux window. The owner retains
the heavy locks and recorder; the driver acquires no nested window lock. Supply
the actual outer installation container PID and the configured listener address.
The driver joins that existing network namespace and creates only a private
mount namespace for hostname resolution. TLS still verifies the advertised
origin against the exported installation CA. Host /etc/hosts is unchanged.

Example parameter names (use actual paths, source and PID from that window):

    python3 installed_workspaces.py \
      --client /absolute/client/ownsolid \
      --client-manifest /absolute/client/client-manifest.json \
      --evidence /absolute/actual/runtime-evidence \
      --expected-control-source ACTUAL_FROZEN_CONTROL_REVISION \
      --network-pid ACTUAL_EXISTING_INSTALLATION_PID \
      --connect-address ACTUAL_LOOPBACK_LISTENER_ADDRESS \
      --result /absolute/new/private/result-directory

The Control revision must match installed-ready and the installed image/binary
provenance. The client revision is separate and may differ. The extracted installed
Control binary and the CLI binary are each checked against their own manifest hash.

CLI cases: list/get, table/JSON/YAML, bounded pages and replay, absent search,
foreign-tenant refusal, search-bound cursor, actionable invalid-input and expired
session messages, nonadministrator Admin login refusal and fresh login recovery.
The runner creates and revokes only its own sessions. It changes no shared account,
membership, workspace, service, database or installation lifecycle.

Portal companion cases are separately labelled: the generated restricted member
can read its own workspace, cannot read the other workspace or foreign tenant,
and logs out. Admin is allowed to see every workspace in the installed tenant;
the report does not call that authority a cross-workspace refusal.

result.json records public provenance, case results, stable error codes and request
IDs. It excludes raw HTTP/CLI output and credentials. It reports installed acceptance
only after all cases and session cleanup pass. The full offline/zero-egress conclusion
belongs to DEL's completed shared recorder window. This handoff itself is not an
installed acceptance result and does not close DEV-102 or activate GW-104.
